        "title": "19th-Century Philosophy - Schopenhauer, Marx, Kierkegaard, Nietzsche",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The 19th century is defined by reactions to Hegel. Hegel's system claimed to show the rational structure of history and reality; his successors asked whether this was wishful thinking or ideological cover. Four major figures, four different revolts:"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-19TH-CENTURY.md#003",
      "path": [
        "07-19TH-CENTURY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:philosophers-thinkers:07-19th-century, git-history:philosophers-thinkers:07-19th-century]",
        "canonical_path": "philosophers-thinkers/07-19TH-CENTURY.md",
        "concepts": "[19th, century]",
        "current_path": "philosophers-thinkers/07-19TH-CENTURY.md",
        "id": "maxim:philosophers-thinkers:19th-century",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "philosophers-thinkers",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[19th, century]",
        "section": "philosophers-thinkers",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "19th-Century Philosophy - Schopenhauer, Marx, Kierkegaard, Nietzsche",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  HEGEL'S SYSTEM\n  \"History is the development of Spirit toward freedom.\n   The actual is the rational.\"\n         │\n         ├── SCHOPENHAUER (1788–1860) ─── Inverts Hegel\n         │   \"Reality is blind, irrational Will.\n         │    History is repetitive suffering.\"\n         │\n         ├── MARX (1818–1883) ─────────── Materializes Hegel\n         │   \"History is class struggle, not Spirit.\n         │    Material conditions determine consciousness.\"\n         │\n         ├── KIERKEGAARD (1813–1855) ──── Subjectifies Hegel\n         │   \"The individual, not the system.\n         │    Existence cannot be captured by abstraction.\"\n         │\n         └── NIETZSCHE (1844–1900) ─────── Diagnoses Hegel\n             \"Hegel's progress is a secular Christian narrative.\n              Kill God, revalue all values, will to power.\"\n```"
    }
